sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Coordinator as CustomerQueueCoordinator
    participant Worker as EventWorker
    participant Store as EventProcessingStore
    participant Inbox as Event Inbox
    participant Failure as FailureSimulator
    participant Tenant as TenantConfigService
    participant Preference as UserPreferenceService
    participant Factory as NotificationServiceFactory
    participant Provider as Channel Provider
    participant Processed as Processed Event Store
    participant Backlog as BacklogTracker

    Coordinator->>Worker: processNext(customerKey)
    Worker->>Store: claimHead(customerKey, now)
    Store->>Inbox: find lowest unresolved sequence

    alt no unresolved event
        Store-->>Worker: NOTHING
        Worker-->>Coordinator: NOTHING
    else head is DLQ
        Store-->>Worker: BLOCKED
        Worker-->>Coordinator: BLOCKED
    else retry time is in future
        Store-->>Worker: WAIT(delay)
        Worker-->>Coordinator: WAIT(delay)
        Coordinator->>Coordinator: schedule customer after delay
    else eligible head exists
        Store->>Inbox: mark RUNNING and increment attempt
        Store-->>Worker: CLAIMED(event)
        Worker->>Worker: parse payload
        Worker->>Failure: maybeFail(event)
        Worker->>Tenant: require enabled channel config
        Worker->>Factory: providerFor(channel)
        Factory-->>Worker: channel provider
        Worker->>Provider: validate(payload)
        Worker->>Preference: resolve preference
        Worker->>Worker: enrich payload and choose outcome
        Worker->>Store: complete(event, result)
        Store->>Processed: insert if eventId absent
        Store->>Inbox: mark PROCESSED
        Worker->>Backlog: release()
        Worker-->>Coordinator: ADVANCE
        Coordinator->>Coordinator: signal same customer for next event
    end

    Note over Coordinator,Worker: Different customer keys can run on different workers in parallel.
    Note over Store,Inbox: Only the lowest unresolved sequence can be claimed.
